From: CervantesHallo <227578309+CervantesHallo@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winmm: Defer format probes until waveform capabilities are requested.

Mixer initialization needs endpoint metadata, not waveform format masks.
Keep the existing shared-format probes, but run them for the requested
endpoint into a local capability copy. Use a local COM enumerator and
propagate resolution, activation and operational probe failures instead
of reporting a successful empty mask. Mapper behavior and ANSI delegation
are preserved; short A/W requests skip probing unless the complete format
DWORD is requested. Shared capability metadata is never updated by a probe.

Serialize initialization with InitOnce. Stage both endpoint lists, unwind
failed attempts for retry, and publish complete metadata before registering
notifications. Successful empty enumeration remains retryable. Missing
defaults retain all endpoints in collection order.

Base-source: dlls/winmm/waveform.c
